CD        CD [drive:][path] - Show or change the current directory.
COPY         COPY source[+source...] [destination] [/A | /B] [/V] [/Y | /-Y]
    /A selects text handling, /B binary handling, and /V verifies writes.
    COPYCMD presets overwrite behavior. The last explicit switch wins.
DEL       DEL [drive:][path]filename [/P] [/Q] - /Q skips bulk confirmation and /P prompts for each file.
DELTREE   DELTREE [/Y] path [path...] - Delete a directory tree. /Y skips confirmation.
DIR          DIR [path] [/A[:attrs]] [/B] [/L] [/O[:order]] [/P] [/S] [/W]
    Attributes D=directory, R=read-only, H=hidden, S=system, A=archive.
    Sort keys N=name, E=extension, S=size, D=date, G=directories first.
    Prefix an attribute with - to exclude it or a sort key to reverse it.
    /B bare names, /L lowercase, /P page, /S recurse, /W wide.
    DIRCMD sets defaults. /- cancels a preset switch.
FORMAT       FORMAT drive: [/Q] [/V[:label]] [/S] [/B] [/F:size]
    /Q quick formats, /V sets the label, /S transfers DOS system files.
    /B reserves system space. /F selects a supported floppy size.
    The parser also recognizes /T and /N for geometry and /1, /4 and /8.
HELP      HELP [command] - List topics or display a command summary. Use HELP | MORE to page.
MD        MD [drive:]path - Create a directory.
MEM       MEM [/C | /CLASSIFY | /D | /DEBUG] [/P] - Show memory usage, optionally with paging.
MORE      MORE [filename] - Page a text file or piped input.
MOVE      MOVE [/Y | /-Y] source[,source...] destination - Move files or rename a directory. /-Y asks before overwriting.
RD        RD [drive:]path - Remove an empty directory.
REN       REN [drive:][path]oldname newname - Rename files.
TYPE      TYPE [drive:][path]filename - Display a text file.
XCOPY        XCOPY source [destination] [/A | /M] [/D:date] [/P] [/S] [/E] [/V] [/W]
    /A selects archive files, /M also clears their archive bits.
    /D filters by date, /P prompts, /V verifies, /W waits before starting.
    /S includes subdirectories. /E with /S includes empty directories.
    XCOPYCMD sets defaults. Explicit switches, including /-S and /-E, win.
CHDIR     CD [drive:][path] - Show or change the current directory.
ERASE     Alias for DEL. /Q skips bulk confirmation and /P prompts for each file.
MKDIR     MD [drive:]path - Create a directory.
RMDIR     RD [drive:]path - Remove an empty directory.
RENAME    REN [drive:][path]oldname newname - Rename files.
/?        HELP [command] - List topics or display a command summary. Use HELP | MORE to page.

CONFIG.SYS drivers and support files
ANSI.SYS     DEVICE=ANSI.SYS [/X] [/L] [/K] - Add ANSI console support.
DISPLAY.SYS  DEVICE=DISPLAY.SYS CON[:]=(type[,hwcp[,n]])
    Select display type, hardware code page and software code-page slots.
    The parser also accepts a parenthesized hardware page and (n,m) counts.
DRIVER.SYS   DEVICE=DRIVER.SYS /D:drive [/F:type] [/H:heads] [/S:sectors]
    [/T:tracks] [/C] - Add a logical floppy drive. /D selects the physical unit.
EMM386.SYS   DEVICE=EMM386.SYS [size] [Mx] [ON | OFF | AUTO]
    Size is in KB. Mx selects the page-frame mapping. AUTO enables on demand.
PRINTER.SYS  DEVICE=PRINTER.SYS LPT#[:]=(type[,hwcp[,n]])
    Select printer type, hardware code page(s) and software page slots.
    Use a parenthesized list to give multiple hardware code pages.
RAMDRIVE.SYS DEVICE=RAMDRIVE.SYS [KB] [sector-size] [entries] [/E | /A]
    /E uses extended memory, /A uses expanded memory. /U is hardware-specific.
SMARTDRV.SYS Load with DEVICE= to install the disk cache.
UMBS.SYS     DEVICE=UMBS.SYS start-end [...] - Supply mapped RAM as UMBs. Use hexadecimal segment addresses and exclusive end addresses.
VDISK.SYS    DEVICE=VDISK.SYS [KB] [sector-size] [entries] [/E[:sectors]]
    Defaults are 64 KB, 128 bytes per sector and 64 directory entries.
    /E uses extended memory. Optional transfer count is 1-8 (default 8).
XMAEM.SYS    DEVICE=XMAEM.SYS [KB] - Emulate XMA on supported hardware.
XMA2EMS.SYS  Provide EMS services using XMA memory.
COUNTRY.SYS  Country data selected by the CONFIG.SYS COUNTRY= directive.
KEYBOARD.SYS Keyboard layout data used by KEYB.

Additional commands
APPEND       APPEND [path[;path...]] [/X[:ON|OFF]] [/PATH:ON|OFF] [/E]
    /X extends which operations use APPEND. /PATH controls explicit paths.
    /E stores the list in the environment. APPEND ; clears the list.
ASSIGN       ASSIGN [x=y ...] [/STATUS | /STA]
    Run without mappings to reset assignments. /STATUS lists mappings.
ATTRIB       ATTRIB [+R|-R] [+A|-A] [path] [/S]
    /S includes subdirectories. R is read-only and A is archive.
BACKUP       BACKUP source target [/S] [/M] [/A] [/D:date] [/T:time]
    Additional switches are /L[:logfile] and /F[:size].
    /S includes subdirectories, /M selects changed files, /A appends.
    /D and /T select by date and time. /L logs and /F formats media.
BREAK      BREAK [ON|OFF] - Control extended Ctrl+C checking.
CALL       CALL batchfile [arguments] - Run a nested batch file.
CHCP       CHCP [codepage] - Display or change the active code page.
CHKDSK       CHKDSK [drive:][path] [/F] [/V]
    /F repairs filesystem errors. /V lists files as they are checked.
CLS        Clear the display.
COMMAND    Start another command interpreter.
COMP       Compare files. /D shows decimal bytes, /A characters, /L line numbers, /N=n limits lines, /C ignores ASCII case.
CTTY       CTTY device - Change the command interpreter console.
DATE       DATE [date] - Display or set the date.
DEBUG      Inspect and modify memory and run machine-code programs.
DISKCOMP   Compare two floppy disks.
DISKCOPY   Copy a floppy disk. /V verifies destination tracks.
ECHO       ECHO [ON|OFF|message] - Control batch echoing or print a message.
EDLIN        EDLIN filename [/B] - Edit a text file. /B ignores Ctrl+Z.
EXE2BIN    Convert an eligible EXE image to binary form.
EXIT       Leave the current command interpreter.
FASTOPEN     FASTOPEN [drive:[entries] ...] [/X] - Cache file and directory lookups.
    /X uses expanded memory.
FC           FC [/A] [/B] [/C] [/L] [/LBn] [/N] [/T] [/W] [/n] file1 file2
    /A abbreviates output, /B selects binary comparison, /L selects text.
    /C ignores case, /N numbers lines, /T preserves tabs, /W ignores whitespace.
    /LBn sets the line buffer limit. /n sets the resynchronization match length.
FDISK      Manage fixed-disk partitions. /STATUS reports disk usage and /MBR restores master boot code.
FIND         FIND [/V] [/C] [/N] [/I] "text" [files...]
    /V selects nonmatches, /C counts, /N numbers lines, /I ignores case.
FOR        Run a command for each item in a set.
GOTO       GOTO label - Continue a batch file at the named label.
GRAFTABL     GRAFTABL [codepage | /STATUS | /STA]
    Load a graphics character table or display the currently loaded table.
GRAPHICS     GRAPHICS [type] [/R] [/B] [/LCD] [/PRINTBOX:name | /PB:name]
    /R reverses the image, /B includes the background, /LCD selects LCD.
IF         Execute a batch command conditionally. IF [NOT] DIREXIST path command tests for a directory.
JOIN         JOIN [drive: path | drive: /D] - Join a drive to a directory or undo it.
KEYB         KEYB [layout[,codepage[,file]]] [/ID:id]
    Select a keyboard layout, optionally by keyboard ID.
LABEL      Display, set, or remove a disk volume label.
LH         Run an external program in upper memory when available.
LOADFIX    LOADFIX program [arguments] - Run a program above the first 64 KiB.
LOADHIGH   Run an external program in upper memory when available.
MBASIC     Start the BASIC interpreter.
MODE         MODE [device] [/STATUS | /STAT | /STA]
    Configure display modes, serial ports, printer ports or code pages.
NLSFUNC    Load national-language support.
PATH       Display or set the executable search path.
PAUSE      Suspend batch execution until a key is pressed.
PRINT        PRINT [files...] [/D:device] [/B:size] [/Q:count]
    [/S:ticks] [/U:ticks] [/M:ticks] [/T] [/C] [/P]
    /D selects a device. /B and /Q size the buffer and queue.
    /S, /U and /M adjust timing. /T clears the queue.
    /C cancels listed files and /P adds listed files.
PROMPT     Change the command prompt.
RECOVER    Recover readable data from a file or disk.
REM        Add a comment to a batch file.
REPLACE      REPLACE source [destination] [/A] [/P] [/R] [/S] [/U] [/W]
    /A adds new files, /P prompts, /R permits replacing read-only files.
    /S includes subdirectories, /U replaces older files, /W waits for a disk.
RESTORE      RESTORE source-drive: [destination] [/S] [/P] [/M] [/N] [/D]
    [/B:date] [/A:date] [/E:time] [/L:time]
    /S includes subdirectories, /P prompts, /M selects modified files.
    /N selects missing files. /D lists matches without restoring.
    /B and /A filter by date, and /E and /L filter by time.
SELECT     Run the DOS setup utility.
SET        Display or change environment variables.
SHARE        SHARE [/F:bytes] [/L:locks] [/NC]
    /F sizes file space, /L sets lock count, /NC disables sharing checks.
SHIFT      Shift the batch positional arguments.
SORT         SORT [/R] [/+column] - Sort input. /R reverses the order.
SUBST        SUBST [drive: path | drive: /D] - Map a drive or remove its mapping.
SYS        Transfer DOS system files to a disk.
TIME       TIME [time] - Display or set the time.
TREE         TREE [drive:][path] [/F] [/A] - /F includes files, /A uses ASCII.
TRUENAME   Display the canonical path for a file or directory.
VER        Display the DOS version.
VERIFY     VERIFY [ON|OFF] - Control verification of disk writes.
VI         Start the screen editor.
VOL        Display the disk volume label.

CONFIG.SYS directives
BREAK=     Enable or disable extended Ctrl+C checking.
BUFFERS=   Set the number of disk buffers.
COMMENT=   Change the CONFIG.SYS comment character.
COUNTRY=   Select country and code-page information.
CPSW=      Configure code-page switching.
DEVICE=    Load a device driver with optional arguments.
DEVICEHIGH= Try loading a driver in upper memory, with conventional memory as fallback.
DOS=       HIGH moves selected DOS routines into the HMA. UMB enables upper memory. Both can be combined.
DRIVPARM=  Override drive parameters. The geometry table supports format codes through /F:7.
FCBS=      FCBS=n,m sets the FCB count and protected count.
FILES=     Set the maximum number of open files.
INSTALL=   Run an executable during configuration.
LASTDRIVE= Set the highest drive letter.
MULTITRACK= Configure multitrack disk I/O.
SHELL=     Select the command interpreter and its arguments.
SHELLHIGH= Try placing the interpreter and permanent environment in upper memory.
STACKS=    STACKS=n,size sets the number and size of interrupt stacks.
SWITCHES=  /K selects conventional keyboard handling.
